---
import { getEntry } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const contact = (await getEntry("contact", "contact"))!.data;
const email = contact.enquiry_email || contact.email;
const updated = "19 October 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="When and how you get your money back on a GrintByte product."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Refund policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose-grint mt-8 space-y-8 text-base leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        At GrintByte, we want to ensure you are completely satisfied with our software products. We
        stand behind our work, and if a product does not function as intended, we are here to
        assist.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">1. 14-day money-back guarantee</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We offer a 14-day refund policy on all initial software license purchases. If our
          software fails to function on your system as advertised, or contains critical defects
          that our team cannot resolve, you are entitled to a full refund within 14 days of your
          purchase date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">2. Refund conditions</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">To be eligible for a refund, we ask that you:</p>
        <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            Contact our support team first to describe the issue you encountered, allowing us an
            opportunity to provide a fix or configuration guidance.
          </li>
          <li>
            Provide necessary diagnostic details (such as error logs, platform version or
            environment specifications) so we can verify the technical limitation.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">3. Exclusions</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Refunds will generally not be granted under the following circumstances:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>The 14-day evaluation window from the date of purchase has passed.</li>
          <li>
            You decided not to use the software without experiencing any technical fault or
            functional limitation.
          </li>
          <li>
            The issue arises from unsupported server environments, custom modifications made to
            our code by you, or incompatibility with unverified third-party extensions.
          </li>
          <li>
            Automatic renewals of ongoing subscriptions, where offered, unless canceled prior to
            the renewal billing cycle.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">4. How to request a refund</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Because transactions are processed via our Merchant of Record:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            You can submit a refund request by contacting us at
            <a href={`mailto:${email}`} class="text-brand underline">{email}</a> with your Lemon
            Squeezy order number and purchase email address.
          </li>
          <li>
            Alternatively, you can manage your purchase or raise an issue directly through your
            Lemon Squeezy customer receipt portal.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Once approved, refunds are processed immediately and typically reflect on your original
          payment method within 5 to 10 business days, depending on your bank or payment provider.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
